 "title": "Sentence patterns",
 "intro": "Yes. Persian grammar books sort simple sentences by how many parts the verb needs: two, three or four. That gives seven basic patterns (one with two parts, three with three, three with four), close to the five to seven that English grammars list. The parts are the same as in English. The big difference is the order: Farsi puts the verb last.",
