  {
   "title": "The hidden ‑e that links words",
   "text": "A noun is joined to a word that describes it, or to its owner, by an ‑e sound called ezafe (‑ye after a vowel). After a consonant it is said but usually not written (shown here with a small mark: کتابِ خوب); after a vowel it is written ی: خانه‌ی علی.",
